1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,700
Most shop tools show a red bar. A red bar is not a reason. Takt
tells you why you're late, and what would fix it.

2
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:16,860
High-mix shops don't lose dates because one operation is slow. Jobs
wait behind a constrained work center, and that queue is where the
promise disappears.

3
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:32,360
Takt opens on the diagnosis board. Job J-1051 is 26h 40m late. Every
minute traces to queue time at CNC-02, running at 91% load. Named.
Measured. Causal.

4
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:44,210
Test the fix before you spend. Add one machine at CNC-02. Same seed,
one capacity change. The late job clears, and all 1,600 lost minutes
come back.

5
00:00:44,590 --> 00:00:54,410
The floor is real, too. Search the job book, filter by status, copy
the rows as CSV. No fake export buttons. No dead controls.

6
00:00:54,790 --> 00:01:03,980
Accounts are optional. A guest key opens the shop instantly. Sign
in, and every workspace stays separate, with its own people and
data.

7
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:18,590
Authority is enforced on the Serverpod API, not the interface.
Owner, editor, viewer. A viewer reads the board; the server rejects
every write. Hiding a button is UX. Rejecting the write is security.

8
00:01:18,970 --> 00:01:28,860
Takt is Flutter and Serverpod, with real auth, real Postgres, 30
server tests, and 17 Flutter tests. The scheduler that tells you why
you're late.
